263	// resolveDirectiveOrder merges the baseline directive order with the
264	// before/after/first/last constraints of one adaptation into a single stable
265	// order. The constraints form a directed graph of user declarations only;
266	// the baseline is not part of that graph, it only supplies the traversal
267	// order. Baseline directives are emitted in their default order, but before
268	// a directive is emitted every directive constrained to run before it is
269	// pulled up recursively, so a reordered directive lands adjacent to its
270	// anchor (like a single insertion) while transitive constraints are honored.
271	// Because graph construction never depends on the sequence in which the
272	// constraints were collected, swapping declaration lines, import traversal
273	// order or glob order cannot change the result as long as the constraint
274	// set is equivalent. Directives unrelated to the constraints keep their
275	// default positions.
